findings.body:
`formatStudiesText` formats `strings.detailTextStudies`, which is the old v1 copy ("may install and run studies from time to time"). The V2 constant `detailTextStudiesV2` is added in the same PR but never reaches this helper. A caller that picks up the helper would show the old text, which contradicts the purpose of this PR. Nothing in the repo calls `SettingsTextFormatter.shared` yet, so the bug is latent.

::code{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="417-431"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The helper is dead code today and its only behaviour is wrong. Either remove it or point it at the V2 constants. Adding a singleton formatter to a `strings` namespace struct also goes against how the rest of this file is written.

::suggestion{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="423-429"}
        func formatStudiesText(appName: String) -> String {
            return String(format: strings.detailTextStudiesV2, appName)
        }

        func formatRolloutsText(appName: String) -> String {
            return String(format: strings.detailTextRollouts, appName)
        }

The new Focus keys `Settings.toggleStudies.v2`, `Settings.detailTextStudies.v2`, `Settings.toggleRollouts`, `Settings.detailTextRollouts`, and `Settings.detailTextSendUsageData.v2` do not appear in any Focus `Localizable.strings`. The grep finds them only in `UIConstants.swift`. Under `NSLocalizedString`, the `value:` argument is used as the fallback, so English users see the new copy. Every other locale falls back to English, and the existing Focus toggles already have translated entries. Once these constants are used, translators will not see them.

::diff{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="203-209"}

::callout{type="info"}
If the Focus v2 strings are meant to stage copy for translation, check whether Focus's l10n pipeline picks up new keys from source automatically. If it does not, add them to the source `Localizable.strings` (en-GB, en-CA) in the same way the Firefox side did.
